      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Sultan Mosque, built in 1824, stands as a monumental symbol of the area’s Islamic heritage and architectural prowess.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ithy.com/article/kampong-glam-heritage-tourism-iea2zt0w",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Kampong Glam still retains strong ties to the Native-Malay and Muslim community, earning it the nickname “Muslim Quarter.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kampong_Glam",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The area’s shophouses are well‑preserved, showcasing traditional Malay design alongside modern elements, reflecting its colonial past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ithy.com/article/kampong-glam-heritage-tourism-iea2zt0w",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
